# MCP OAuth 2.1 Dynamic Client Registration

This rule defines the implementation guidelines for OAuth 2.1 and Dynamic Client Registration (RFC 7591) in the Microsoft 365 MCP Server, following the official MCP specification from https://modelcontextprotocol.io.

## Core Architecture

### MCP Server as Resource Server (NOT Authorization Server)

Per the MCP specification (2025-06-18), MCP servers function as **Resource Servers**, not Authorization Servers:

```
┌────────────────────┐       ┌────────────────────┐       ┌────────────────────┐
│    MCP Client      │◄─────►│    MCP Server      │◄─────►│  Authorization     │
│   (e.g. Cursor)    │       │  (Resource Server) │       │     Server         │
│                    │       │                    │       │  (Microsoft Entra) │
└────────────────────┘       └────────────────────┘       └────────────────────┘
```

**Key responsibilities:**
- MCP Server validates incoming access tokens
- MCP Server provides protected resources (Microsoft Graph API access)
- Authorization Server (Microsoft Entra ID) issues tokens

## Relevant OAuth Standards

This implementation adheres to:

| Standard | RFC/Draft | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| OAuth 2.1 | IETF DRAFT draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-13 | Core OAuth framework |
| Dynamic Client Registration | RFC 7591 | Client registration protocol |
| Authorization Server Metadata | RFC 8414 | Discovery endpoints |
| Protected Resource Metadata | RFC 9728 | Resource server discovery |

## Dynamic Client Registration (RFC 7591)

### Registration Endpoint

The server MUST expose a `/register` endpoint that accepts POST requests with the following structure:

```typescript
// Request body (RFC 7591 Section 2)
interface ClientRegistrationRequest {
  redirect_uris: string[];                    // REQUIRED
  client_name?: string;                       // OPTIONAL
  client_uri?: string;                        // OPTIONAL
  logo_uri?: string;                          // OPTIONAL
  scope?: string;                             // OPTIONAL
  contacts?: string[];                        // OPTIONAL
  tos_uri?: string;                           // OPTIONAL
  policy_uri?: string;                        // OPTIONAL
  jwks_uri?: string;                          // OPTIONAL
  jwks?: object;                              // OPTIONAL
  software_id?: string;                       // OPTIONAL
  software_version?: string;                  // OPTIONAL
  grant_types?: string[];                     // OPTIONAL (default: ["authorization_code"])
  response_types?: string[];                  // OPTIONAL (default: ["code"])
  token_endpoint_auth_method?: string;        // OPTIONAL (default: "none" for public clients)
}

// Response body (RFC 7591 Section 3.2.1)
interface ClientRegistrationResponse {
  client_id: string;                          // REQUIRED
  client_secret?: string;                     // CONDITIONAL (for confidential clients)
  client_id_issued_at?: number;               // OPTIONAL
  client_secret_expires_at?: number;          // REQUIRED if client_secret issued
  redirect_uris: string[];                    // REQUIRED
  grant_types: string[];                      // REQUIRED
  response_types: string[];                   // REQUIRED
  token_endpoint_auth_method: string;         // REQUIRED
  // ... echo back all registered metadata
}
```

### Client Storage

Dynamically registered clients MUST be stored with:
- Unique client_id (UUID v4 recommended)
- Timestamp of registration
- All metadata from registration request
- Optional expiration time

```typescript
interface RegisteredClient {
  client_id: string;
  client_secret?: string;
  client_secret_expires_at?: number;
  client_id_issued_at: number;
  redirect_uris: string[];
  grant_types: string[];
  response_types: string[];
  token_endpoint_auth_method: string;
  client_name?: string;
  scope?: string;
}
```

## Discovery Endpoints

### OAuth Authorization Server Metadata (RFC 8414)

Endpoint: `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`

```json
{
  "issuer": "https://your-server.com",
  "authorization_endpoint": "https://your-server.com/authorize",
  "token_endpoint": "https://your-server.com/token",
  "registration_endpoint": "https://your-server.com/register",
  "response_types_supported": ["code"],
  "response_modes_supported": ["query"],
  "grant_types_supported": ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"],
  "token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported": ["none", "client_secret_post"],
  "code_challenge_methods_supported": ["S256"],
  "scopes_supported": ["User.Read", "Mail.Read", "..."]
}
```

### Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728)

Endpoint: `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`

```json
{
  "resource": "https://your-server.com/mcp",
  "authorization_servers": ["https://your-server.com"],
  "scopes_supported": ["User.Read", "Mail.Read", "..."],
  "bearer_methods_supported": ["header"],
  "resource_documentation": "https://your-server.com"
}
```

## Implementation Guidelines

### 1. MicrosoftOAuthProvider Extension

The `MicrosoftOAuthProvider` class should implement:

```typescript
import { ProxyOAuthServerProvider } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/auth/providers/proxyProvider.js';

export class MicrosoftOAuthProvider extends ProxyOAuthServerProvider {
  private registeredClients: Map<string, RegisteredClient> = new Map();

  async registerClient(request: ClientRegistrationRequest): Promise<ClientRegistrationResponse> {
    // Validate redirect_uris
    // Generate unique client_id
    // Store client metadata
    // Return registration response
  }

  async getClient(clientId: string): Promise<RegisteredClient | null> {
    // Return registered client or null
  }
}
```

### 2. Token Validation

Access tokens MUST be validated by:
1. Checking token format (JWT or opaque)
2. Verifying with Microsoft Graph API (`/me` endpoint)
3. Extracting user context for request handling

```typescript
verifyAccessToken: async (token: string): Promise<AuthInfo> => {
  const response = await fetch('https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
  });
  
  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Token verification failed: ${response.status}`);
  }
  
  return {
    token,
    clientId: extractClientId(token),
    scopes: extractScopes(token),
  };
}
```

### 3. PKCE Support (Required for Public Clients)

Public clients (without client_secret) MUST use PKCE:

```typescript
// code_challenge_method: S256
const codeVerifier = generateCodeVerifier();  // 43-128 characters
const codeChallenge = base64url(sha256(codeVerifier));
```

### 4. Scope Management

Scopes should map to Microsoft Graph permissions:

```typescript
const SCOPE_MAPPING = {
  'User.Read': 'Basic user profile',
  'Mail.Read': 'Read user mail',
  'Mail.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user mail',
  'Calendars.Read': 'Read user calendars',
  'Files.Read': 'Read user files',
  // ... additional scopes
};
```

## Error Handling

### Registration Errors (RFC 7591 Section 3.2.2)

```typescript
interface RegistrationError {
  error: 'invalid_redirect_uri' | 'invalid_client_metadata' | 'invalid_software_statement';
  error_description?: string;
}
```

### Token Errors (RFC 6749 Section 5.2)

```typescript
interface TokenError {
  error: 'invalid_request' | 'invalid_client' | 'invalid_grant' | 
         'unauthorized_client' | 'unsupported_grant_type';
  error_description?: string;
}
```

## Security Requirements

### MUST Implement:
- [ ] HTTPS for all endpoints in production
- [ ] PKCE for all public clients
- [ ] Token validation via Microsoft Graph API
- [ ] Secure storage of client secrets
- [ ] Rate limiting on registration endpoint
- [ ] Input validation with Zod schemas

### SHOULD Implement:
- [ ] Client credential rotation
- [ ] Registration access tokens for client management
- [ ] Audit logging for all OAuth operations

### MUST NOT:
- [ ] Store tokens in logs
- [ ] Accept redirect_uris with localhost in production (except for development)
- [ ] Skip token validation

## Cursor Integration

When integrating with Cursor IDE:

1. **MCP Server Login:**
   ```bash
   cursor-agent mcp login <server-name>
   ```

2. **List MCP Tools:**
   ```bash
   cursor-agent mcp list-tools
   ```

3. **Configuration in `.cursor/mcp.json`:**
   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "ms365": {
         "url": "https://your-server.com/mcp",
         "transportType": "streamable-http"
       }
     }
   }
   ```

